1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Well, how do you go about making a small rowboat?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:11,000
We just make the small scale model and draft it from that.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Make a keel out.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
You make a scale model first?

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Most everybody does, make a scale model.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Or else they draft them out, draw them out on paper.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Either one you want to, it doesn't matter.

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
How big are these scale models?

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
A general rule on small type.

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Oh, just a three-quarter inch to a foot.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:43,500
The large ones are up to a quarter inch to a foot.

12
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:47,500
And what's the purpose of the scale model?

13
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:50,500
Well, to determine the length and the width and all this.

14
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:59,000
Oh, I see. They just use smaller everything and then they just scale them up and down.

15
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,000
And then...

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
And how do you go about deciding to build the boat itself?

17
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Well, you make the keel first from the model, from the drafting, drawing, what I did.

18
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Then you make the stem and the stern.

19
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
And for the small stuff, the small boats where you bend the frame,

20
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,000
you make a mold, what we call a mold, so there's sections of it.

21
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
At the so far top on the boat, you take the...

22
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
the shape of it, make sections.

23
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
What do they use to do that, plywood?

24
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Plywood or cedar, either, doesn't matter.
